Usage Licence for SpaceSonar

This text applies to the versions it ships with, which name the version
number. Older versions carry the licence they were released with.

This licence is provided in English and German. The German version below is
the binding one; the English text is a translation for convenience.

The provider is the operator named in the legal notice (Impressum) of
appsonar.de.

1. Use. You may install and use this version of SpaceSonar free of charge,
   privately and at work, on any number of devices and without a time limit.
2. Other versions. This licence applies to the version named above. Other
   versions come with their own terms. Your right to use this version
   remains unaffected. There is no entitlement to updates or support.
3. Distribution. You may link to the download page on appsonar.de. You may
   not pass on, sell, rent out or offer the app itself for download without
   consent. Copies for your own use and for backup are permitted.
4. Modification. You may not modify or reverse engineer the app or use parts
   of it, except where the law permits it. Statutory rights, in particular
   under sections 69d and 69e of the German Copyright Act (UrhG), remain
   unaffected.
5. Third-party components. Software of other providers contained in the app
   is subject to their licences. For these components, their licences take
   precedence over clauses 3 and 4.
6. Your files. The app works with your files and can move, rename or delete
   them on your instruction. Back up important data regularly.
7. Use at your own risk, exclusion of liability. The app is provided free of
   charge and without any promise as to function, freedom from errors or
   fitness for a purpose. You use it at your own risk. Any liability of the
   provider is excluded, including for loss of data. The only exceptions are
   cases in which the law prohibits the exclusion: intent, gross negligence,
   fraudulent concealment of defects, injury to life, body or health, and
   claims under the German Product Liability Act.
8. Law. German law applies. Mandatory consumer protection provisions of the
   country in which you live as a consumer remain unaffected.

